# 14x8 top-down desk (slimmed 16x9 -> 14x8 for laptop density: ONE keyboard
# row, two right surface columns trimmed; monitor/keyboard/cup all keep their
# reads). Row 0 is the raised monitor bezel that RISES 1px above the desk back
# (blitted at desk.y-1, see DeskCubicle in drawable.rs) so the screen reads as
# a standing display. Screen uses `j` (dark) so the lime screen-glow overlay
# reads as "workstation active" by contrast. The sprite deliberately overhangs
# the 10x5 ground footprint (DESK_W/DESK_H, invariant #6) by 4px of width: the
# divider column (desk.x + DESK_W + 3) lands exactly on the sprite's last
# column, pinned by `desk_sprite_width_tracks_the_footprint_overhang`.
@frame 0
. . . M M M M M M M M . . .
D D D M M M M M M M M D D D
D D D M j j j j j j M D D D
D D D M j j j j j j M D D D
D D D D n n n n n n D D D D
d d d d d d d d d d d d d d
D k k k k k k k k k D D K D
d d d d d d d d d d d d d d
